WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.360
You can't use a crane kick to&nbsp;
solve all of life's problems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.200
but you can come close. The ending&nbsp;
of "Cobra Kai" season 5 proves it.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.240
After five seasons, it seems that Cobra&nbsp;
Kai's dojo war may finally be over.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.560
Terry Silver monopolized karate classes in&nbsp;
the valley just in time to get sent to prison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.600
and his students departed in a mass&nbsp;
exodus after discovering that he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.320
both a cheater and a felon. While it's unclear&nbsp;
exactly what will become of his many dojos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.400
it seems that he won't be around to continue&nbsp;
teaching his abusive style to kids any time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.680
soon. Additionally, Johnny and Daniel's rivalry&nbsp;
is mostly quenched by the time Season 5 starts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.400
and they become true friends by the finale.&nbsp;
So the dojo war must be over... right?

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.680
Well, that still remains to be&nbsp;
seen. By the end of Season 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.520
there are basically no kids left to&nbsp;
carry on the tradition of evil karate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.840
Tory, Kenny, and Devon — the last three main&nbsp;
characters enrolled in the dojo — all repent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.240
for their harmful ways and make amends with&nbsp;
the good guys by the time Episode 10 concludes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.640
It seems certain that Silver will serve hard time&nbsp;
for his crimes, and while John Kreese does escape&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.200
from prison by the end of Season 5, he's in no&nbsp;
position to start teaching again. Still, some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:09.040
things remain murky. Will Kreese somehow reclaim&nbsp;
the dojos? Will Johnny? Will new evil sensei Kim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.360
Da-Eun take the reins? The war may be over,&nbsp;
but there's still the aftermath to deal with.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.840
For most of the finale, it's implied that&nbsp;
John Kreese might be dead after a brutal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:21.360
stabbing in prison. And given the widespread&nbsp;
harm Kreese has wrought throughout his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.160
an unceremonious end of that&nbsp;
nature almost seems fitting.

00:01:24.291 --> 00:01:27.891
"Sweep the Leg."

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.400
However, the final scene of "Season 5"&nbsp;
shows that Kreese is still very much alive.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.560
After besting a number of his fellow inmates&nbsp;
in a brawl, Kreese earns their loyalty.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.640
This allows him to stage a fake stabbing.&nbsp;
When two of the other prisoners start arguing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.320
Kreese makes a show of getting in between&nbsp;
them to stop the fight, but his only reward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.880
is what appears to be a fatal attack. After&nbsp;
being taken into a less secure medical area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.040
it's revealed that the blood on his shirt&nbsp;
isn't blood, but red Jell-O — a callback to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.200
earlier in the season. The only way this plan&nbsp;
would have worked is if both arguing prisoners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.600
were in on it from the start, which seems to&nbsp;
be the implication. Kreese then dispatches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.160
the surrounding guards and escapes using a&nbsp;
keycard stolen from the prison psychologist.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.480
With Terry Silver likely heading to jail himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:13.440
Kreese looks primed to return as the Big Bad of&nbsp;
the show going forward. However, he also seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.280
to genuinely want a shot at redemption.&nbsp;
It remains to be seen if he'll get one.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.000
The shadow of Pat Morita's Mr. Miyagi&nbsp;
has always loomed large over "Cobra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.880
Kai." His absence is particularly felt in Season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:28.800
5 because of Terry Silver's expanded&nbsp;
role as the show's ultimate villain.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.960
Any fan of "The Karate Kid" would probably&nbsp;
put good money on a prime Mr. Miyagi having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.200
the edge on any of the "Cobra Kai" characters&nbsp;
in a fair fight, but he's sadly not around to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.840
stand up against Silver. Or is he? Over the&nbsp;
course of Season 5, Silver defeats both Daniel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:46.480
LaRusso and Chozen Toguchi in one-on-one&nbsp;
duels. Though Chozen is still decently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.440
inebriated when he faces Silver, and Daniel is&nbsp;
completely ambushed. But in the season finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.760
Daniel is victorious in his rematch, thanks&nbsp;
to Chozen having softened him up beforehand.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:03:00.560
In the end, it takes both Daniel and Chozen&nbsp;
to take Silver down, which is kind of poetic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.680
As the two most direct descendants&nbsp;
of Mr. Miyagi's karate style,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.440
they combine to form some approximation&nbsp;
of what the old master was capable of.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.600
In this way, it's almost like Mr. Miyagi&nbsp;
himself defeats Silver and Cobra Kai,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.440
which makes it especially significant that Daniel&nbsp;
finishes the villain off with a crane kick.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.800
From the start, "Cobra Kai" has been a show&nbsp;
about rivals and rivalries. Johnny re-opens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:25.280
the Cobra Kai dojo because he's still not over&nbsp;
losing to Daniel in "The Karate Kid." Daniel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.280
in turn, starts training new Miyagi-Do&nbsp;
students because of the same rivalry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.800
As the show progresses, numerous other&nbsp;
storylines emerge in the same vein,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:36.560
from Miguel and Robby's mutual hatred&nbsp;
to the beef between Sam and Tory.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:41.120
By the end of "Cobra Kai" Season 5, pretty&nbsp;
much all of those rivalries have melted away.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:45.920
Daniel and Johnny are friends, Miguel and&nbsp;
Robby make amends, Tory and Sam join forces,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:50.640
and even the dojo war itself seems to end with&nbsp;
the arrest of Terry Silver. Even the smaller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:54.960
rivalries, like the one between Robby and Kenny&nbsp;
Payne, are quashed by the end of the season.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.120
With Kreese escaping from prison, there's still&nbsp;
a potentially villainous force on the loose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:03.120
but "Cobra Kai" might be better off exploring&nbsp;
a different kind of rivalry going forward.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.680
The main storyline still left hanging at the end&nbsp;
of Season 5 is the international karate tournament&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:12.960
known as the Sekai Taikai, to which all three main&nbsp;
"Cobra Kai" dojos are invited. For a while, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:16.880
looked like the show's main rivalries would play&nbsp;
out there, but now that everyone's friends again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:21.520
the tournament could be even more interesting. A&nbsp;
friendly rivalry can be just as compelling as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:25.600
hateful one, and the characters now have a chance&nbsp;
to learn from each other and become even stronger.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:31.440
There are still some plot threads left dangling in&nbsp;
the wind after the events of "Cobra Kai" Season 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:35.360
but the season finale still manages to feel&nbsp;
like a full-circle moment for the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.920
"Karate Kid" saga. The only thing missing is&nbsp;
an appearance from Hilary Swank's Julie Pierce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.520
star of "The Next Karate Kid." but when&nbsp;
it comes to the original trilogy starring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:48.720
Mr. Miyagi and Daniel LaRusso, "Cobra Kai"&nbsp;
Season 5 ties up pretty much every loose end.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:53.120
The events of the first film are finally and fully&nbsp;
laid to rest with the brotherly bond established&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:58.960
between Daniel and Johnny. Miyagi-Do continues on&nbsp;
to the next generation, and Cobra Kai is defeated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:03.680
"The Karate Kid Part II" also receives a second&nbsp;
pass with Season 5's extensive arc for Chozen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.440
And of course, Daniel finally puts Terry&nbsp;
Silver in his place, facing the trauma he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.000
caused him in his youth and defeating him with&nbsp;
Mr. Miyagi's signature move, the crane kick.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.320
Even the earlier plotlines of "Cobra Kai"&nbsp;
feel mostly wrapped up by the end of Season 5.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:20.640
The original generation of teens — Robby,&nbsp;
Miguel, Sam, and Tory — now have their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:26.000
acolytes in Kenny and Devon, among others. In&nbsp;
this way, Season 5 feels like the end of a cycle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.280
and while there's still an international&nbsp;
tournament to attend, the story feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:33.760
like it's properly entering a new chapter.&nbsp;
Even Mike Barnes gets a bit of redemption.

00:05:33.957 --> 00:05:38.037
"Daniel, If there is one guy in this world that&nbsp;
doesn't owe me an apology, believe me, it's you."

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.920
One of the smaller storylines at&nbsp;
the end of "Cobra Kai" Season 5&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:46.480
involves Chozen's secret love for Kumiko,&nbsp;
the woman he grew up with in Okinawa.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:50.880
Chozen confesses his feelings to Johnny during&nbsp;
their booze-soaked night out in Episode 9,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:55.040
and Johnny leaks the details to Daniel.&nbsp;
After receiving encouragement from them both,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:58.800
Chozen calls Kumiko and confesses some&nbsp;
level of his feelings. But with all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:02.880
excitement that occurs directly after, this&nbsp;
plotline is left hanging after the finale.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.040
It would be cute to see Chozen and Kumiko get a&nbsp;
happy ending together, especially given all they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.920
went through in "The Karate Kid Part II." Chozen&nbsp;
was undoubtedly a terrible person in his youth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:15.440
but that's partially due to the harmful&nbsp;
influences he had in his life. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:20.240
he's clearly repentant and makes a meaningful&nbsp;
redemption journey in "Cobra Kai" Season 5.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:24.800
After surviving an almost fatal duel with Silver,&nbsp;
Chozen definitely deserves some time to rest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.920
and it seems likely that Kumiko&nbsp;
would be interested in joining him.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:30.800
Many of the other big "Cobra Kai"&nbsp;
romance storylines come back to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.520
point of balance by the end of Season 5. Daniel&nbsp;
and Amanda's marriage is stronger than ever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.760
Johnny makes real strides to be a better man&nbsp;
for Carmen, Sam and Miguel get back together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:43.920
and so do Tory and Robby. After so much&nbsp;
drama, it's nice to see everyone happy.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:49.520
Terry Silver gets a big promotion from&nbsp;
co-villain to Big Bad in "Cobra Kai" Season 5,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:54.000
and he presents a very different kind of evil&nbsp;
than that of John Kreese. Measured and calculated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.800
in almost every area of his life, Silver is&nbsp;
obsessed with dominance on a big-picture level.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:03.200
His plans are global, fitting for a man&nbsp;
of his considerable financial resources.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.240
But in the Season 5 finale, we also see the manic&nbsp;
persona Silver wears in "The Karate Kid Part III."

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:13.600
Thomas Ian Griffith truly stands out in Season&nbsp;
5, and he has a particularly great performance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:18.560
in the final episode. You can see something shift&nbsp;
behind Silver's eyes when Johnny, Chozen, and Mike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:23.520
Barnes break into his house, a flicker of the rage&nbsp;
and ego hidden beneath his veneer of civility.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:27.520
At his core, Silver wants an excuse to&nbsp;
fight. It's the reason he leaves his quiet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:32.240
rich life in "Cobra Kai" Season 4 to team up&nbsp;
with Kreese again. All the wealth he's acquired&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:36.400
through nefarious means is hollow without the&nbsp;
ability to demonstrate his actual strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:42.320
so he challenges Chozen to a sword fight. And even&nbsp;
after nearly losing, Silver seems okay with death.

00:07:42.552 --> 00:07:47.832
"I was meant to die on the battlefield. Do it."

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:52.960
To win the fight, he uses a dirty tactic&nbsp;
to defeat Chozen. It's this duplicity in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:57.840
Silver — the claims of honor with the acts of&nbsp;
cowardice — that ultimately leads to his downfall.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:01.280
Perhaps the most shocking thing about&nbsp;
"Cobra Kai" Season 5 is that good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:05.440
truly wins. Nearly every piece of&nbsp;
the story ends in a triumphant way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.200
Silver loses, his students abandon&nbsp;
the dojo, everyone makes amends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:14.000
and nobody dies. It's almost like a fairy&nbsp;
tale, albeit one with a lot more karate.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.280
In the world of "Cobra Kai," though, this&nbsp;
isn't out of place. Throughout the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:22.000
evil has only ever won when employing dirty&nbsp;
strategies. Sam loses "Cobra Kai" Season 4's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.120
All-Valley Tournament because of&nbsp;
a corrupt referee, for instance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:29.280
Silver defeats Chozen with a slice from his&nbsp;
sword while Daniel's friend is distracted.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:33.200
In this world where balance is an absolute&nbsp;
aspirational value, the only thing holding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:38.400
most characters back is their own issues. But&nbsp;
in Season 5, those issues mostly get resolved.

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:43.200
Robby reconnects with his father, who gets his own&nbsp;
life fully together in turn. Sam and Tory admit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:47.840
their past mistakes and move forward, as does&nbsp;
Chozen. And in the final moments of the season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:52.560
the Cobra Kai dojo is defeated by the revelation&nbsp;
that Silver is actually a duplicitous snake.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:57.120
Yes, the good guys win in "Cobra Kai" Season&nbsp;
5, but they win by redeeming the villains, not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:02.000
by dominating them. Silver is the only character&nbsp;
not offered some kind of redemption in the season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.754
and it's no coincidence that he's&nbsp;
also the only one left in chains.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.480
For all the closure provided by the end of "Cobra&nbsp;
Kai" Season 5, there are still some things left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:15.680
unresolved. The biggest hanging storyline involves&nbsp;
the Sekai Taikai, the massive international karate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:19.840
tournament that Miyagi-Do and Eagle Fang will&nbsp;
compete in. That sure sounds like the kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:23.360
of event that would be a perfect send-off&nbsp;
for the show, but that remains to be seen.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:27.280
There are still some lingering questions that&nbsp;
could be answered in a final tournament arc.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:31.040
Julie Pierce, the only major character from the&nbsp;
"Karate Kid" movies yet to appear in the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.320
could finally show up and share&nbsp;
stories about Mr. Miyagi with Daniel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:37.840
Miguel's father could return as the backer&nbsp;
of one of the tournament's other entrants,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:41.200
given his connections to professional&nbsp;
fighting. And, of course, Kreese could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:46.000
show up to screw everyone over, or possibly&nbsp;
to actually redeem himself once and for all.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.080
What makes the international tournament plot so&nbsp;
interesting is the newly mended relationships&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:53.840
between the main characters. It would be&nbsp;
fun to watch Tory and Sam actually bond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:57.903
over a sparring match, or see Miguel and&nbsp;
Robby team up in some kind of two-on-two.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.240
"Cobra Kai" Season 5 is at its best when it lets&nbsp;
the characters really get to know each other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:06.469
and push each other to change for the better.&nbsp;
With luck, we haven't seen the last of that.

